## 2. The Options struct

**`/workspace/repo/crates/biome_rule_options/src/no_excessive_lines_per_file.rs`** (full file):

```rust
use biome_deserialize_macros::{Deserializable, Merge};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use std::num::NonZeroU16;
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, Deserialize, Deserializable, Merge, Eq, PartialEq, Serialize)]
#[cfg_attr(feature = "schema", derive(schemars::JsonSchema))]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase", deny_unknown_fields, default)]
pub struct NoExcessiveLinesPerFileOptions {
    /// The maximum number of lines allowed in a file.
    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::<_>::is_none")]
    pub max_lines: Option<NonZeroU16>,
    /// When this option is set to `true`, blank lines are not counted...
    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::<_>::is_none")]
    pub skip_blank_lines: Option<bool>,
}

impl NoExcessiveLinesPerFileOptions {
    pub const DEFAULT_MAX_LINES: NonZeroU16 = NonZeroU16::new(300).unwrap();
    pub const DEFAULT_SKIP_BLANK_LINES: bool = false;

    pub fn max_lines(&self) -> NonZeroU16 {
        self.max_lines.unwrap_or(Self::DEFAULT_MAX_LINES)
    }
    pub fn skip_blank_lines(&self) -> bool {
        self.skip_blank_lines.unwrap_or(Self::DEFAULT_SKIP_BLANK_LINES)
    }
}
```

Convention: the struct fields are `Option<T>` with defaults defined as associated consts and exposed via accessor methods. The required derives are exactly `Clone, Debug, Default, Deserialize, Deserializable, Merge, Eq, PartialEq, Serialize` + the `schema` cfg for JsonSchema, plus the serde attributes `rename_all = "camelCase", deny_unknown_fields, default`.

